==> hub ready: https://box1.local (and https://onemind.local), box CA sha256 <sha256-or-token>
==> mesh: hub 100.64.0.1; k3s and the NATS leaf listener run on it

OWNER TOKEN (shown once; only its sha256 is stored in /etc/onemind/tokens.yaml):

    <sha256-or-token>

Trust the box CA on your computer: download https://box1.local/v1/tls/ca.crt and check its sha256 is <sha256-or-token>

Join another machine: make a one-time code here (or Add a device on the dashboard), then approve:

    ONEMIND_TOKEN=<owner token> onemind fabric ticket [--role leaf]

Check this hub:  ONEMIND_TOKEN=<owner token> deploy/verify/verify.sh http://127.0.0.1:8080
Hermes agent (contract §7) model credentials, created by the owner at install time:

    sudo k3s kubectl create namespace app-hermes-agent --dry-run=client -o yaml | sudo k3s kubectl apply -f -
    read -rs KEY   # paste the key; it stays out of shell history and the process list
    printf '<PROVIDER>_API_KEY=%s\n' "$KEY" | sudo k3s kubectl -n app-hermes-agent create secret generic hermes-agent-credentials --from-env-file=/dev/stdin

